alert icmp any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"ICMP Ping Detected"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"Possible TCP Port Scan Detected"; flags:S; detection_filter:track_by_src, count 20, seconds 5; sid:1000002; rev:1;)

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 22 (msg:"Possible SSH Brute Force Attempt"; flags:S; detection_filter:track by_src, count 5, seconds 60 sid:1000003; rev:1;)

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 80 (msg:"HTTP Connection Detected"; flags:S; sid:1000004; rev:1;)

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 21 (msg:"FTP Connection Detected"; flags:S; sid:1000005; rev:1;)

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 23 (msg:"Telnet Connection Detected"; flags:S; sid:1000006; rev:1;)

##example

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET 22

means:

- alert -> generate an alert
- tcp -> ibspect TCP traffic
- any any -> any source IP and source port
- $HOME_NET -> your protected network
- 22 -> destination SSH port
- sid:1000003; -> unique Snort rule ID
